"""GTK popup for timur-bar on i3/X11 and GNOME, the same panel the Omarchy bar opens.

  timur-panel              open (or close, if already open) on the Time entry tab
  timur-panel journal      open on the Journal note tab
  timur-panel --yesterday  start on yesterday

The ▶ timer lives in ~/.cache/timur-bar/timer.json (managed by `timur-bar timer`, shared
with the Omarchy panel), so it keeps running with the panel closed and the bar shows it.

One instance: running it again toggles the open window. It reads
~/.cache/timur-bar/state.json and runs `timur-bar` for every change, like
omarchy/Panel.qml. Needs python-gobject and gtk3.

  TIMUR_PANEL_OFFSET  pixels between the top of the monitor and the panel (bar height, default 30)
  TIMUR_WEEK_TARGET   hours you aim to log per week, shown next to the week total (default 40)
"""

